{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104784","id":2427357773,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6QropN","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104784","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104784.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104784.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104784","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104784/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104784/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104784/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/03b793464f78183378b4db50ad4029ece1bcd913","number":104784,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GLTF export: Allow using a PNG or JPEG fallback image","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds a new feature to the glTF exporter where you can specify using a PNG or JPEG image as a fallback:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"520\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-03-29 at 7 08 22 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78cd8e0e-2a72-403e-ae05-516bf7d64de9\" />\r\n\r\nAt GDC, @fire reminded me that this is something we should have, as a sort of follow-up to PR #79314.\r\n\r\nNote: There is a behavior change in the error cases. In master, if an image failed to serialize, it would add nothing to the images array, leading to a situation where the texture image indices of all following images would get messed up. I moved this code to a new function and made it so that in the case of an error, something will always get written, even just an empty placeholder Dictionary, so the indices stay correct.\r\n\r\nNote: The only supported options for the fallback image format are None, PNG, and JPEG. Theoretically one could include multiple extension image formats (ex: DDS, WebP, and PNG) all in one texture. However, this gets complex because the [DDS](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF/tree/main/extensions/2.0/Vendor/MSFT_texture_dds) and [WebP](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF/tree/main/extensions/2.0/Vendor/EXT_texture_webp) extensions don't specify which should take priority if both are present, the only explicitly specified behavior is that the base glTF image is a fallback relative to the extension. If users have a use case that requires multiple extension image formats, they can already in master make one GLTFDocumentExtension class that provides an option which serializes 2 extension image formats into one glTF texture, and then the behavior is the user's extension's responsibility. This PR's fallback options are limited to the scope of base glTF image formats where the behavior is clear.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default"